Security

The application follows least-privilege principles.

Only required fitness permissions should be requested.

Sensitive configuration must remain outside source control.

Performance

Performance-sensitive operations are executed away from the main thread.

Main Thread
 ├── Compose
 └── State

Background
 ├── Room
 ├── Fitness API
 ├── Synchronization
 └── Data Processing

Architecture Principles

Single Responsibility
Separation of Concerns
Dependency Inversion
Repository abstraction
Unidirectional data flow
Reactive state
Local persistence
Lifecycle-aware background work
